{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_y6ijgxxywhf3xjohknp4amrscm4j7222krhrjmbimin47gd22bsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_012kCimBgXy76kS5iXvx3Bku","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write dtoa/strconv differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration test file for a C-to-Rust differential verification project.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust\n(always use absolute paths; the shell cwd is not reliable)\n\nREAD THESE FIRST (mandatory):\n- /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/tests/common/mod.rs   (harness)\n- /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/tests/t00_smoke.rs    (usage example)\n- /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/c_src/src/strconv.c   (C ground truth)\n- the `dtoa_r`, `dtoa`, `freedtoa`, `gethex`, `strtod__unused` and `dtoa_divmax`\n  definitions in /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/c_src/src/dtoa.c\n  (grep for them; the file is 6265 lines — read only the relevant regions and the\n  doc comment above `dtoa_r` which documents every `mode`)\n\nYOUR TASK: create exactly one new file\n  /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/tests/t04_dtoa.rs\n\nIt must start with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\n```\n\n`duo()` returns `&'static Duo` with `.c` / `.rs` (`Lib`). Already declared:\n```rust\ndtoa_r: unsafe extern \"C\" fn(f64, c_int, c_int, *mut c_int, *mut c_int,\n                            *mut *mut c_char, *mut c_char, usize) -> *mut c_char,\ndtoa:   unsafe extern \"C\" fn(f64, c_int, c_int, *mut c_int, *mut c_int,\n                            *mut *mut c_char) -> *mut c_char,\nfreedtoa:       unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_char),\ngethex:         unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut *const c_char, *mut U, c_int, c_int),\nstrtod__unused: unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, *mut *mut c_char) -> f64,\njsonp_dtostr:   unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_char, usize, f64, c_int) -> c_int,\njsonp_strtod:   unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut strbuffer_t, *mut f64) -> c_int,\nstrbuffer_init / strbuffer_close / strbuffer_append_bytes  (see harness)\njsonp_free:     unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void),\n```\nplus `#[repr(C)] pub union U { pub d: f64, pub L: [u32; 2] }` with `U::zero()` and\n`U::bits()`, and `strbuffer_t` with `strbuffer_t::zeroed()`.\n\nCRITICAL NOTES\n- `dtoa_r`/`dtoa` return a `char*`. When `buf != NULL` the result points INTO `buf`;\n  when `buf == NULL` it is heap-allocated by that library and MUST be released with\n  the SAME library's `freedtoa`. `dtoa` reuses a per-library static result, which the\n  next `dtoa` call frees automatically.\n- Compare: NULL-ness of the return value, the returned NUL-terminated digit string,\n  `*decpt`, `*sign`, and `*rve` as an OFFSET (`rve - returned_ptr`), never as a raw\n  pointer. Initialise `decpt`/`sign` to sentinels (e.g. -424242) so you also detect\n  \"not written\".\n- `gethex` mutates `*sp` (advances it) and `*rvp`. Compare the resulting `*sp` as an\n  OFFSET from the original string start, and `*rvp` via `U::bits()` (raw bit pattern,\n  so NaN payloads and -0.0 are compared exactly).\n- `strtod__unused` returns a double — compare `to_bits()`, and compare `*se` as an\n  OFFSET from the input pointer (handle `se == NULL`).\n- `jsonp_dtostr` writes into a caller buffer. Fill the buffer with a 0xAA sentinel\n  first and compare the RETURN VALUE and the WHOLE buffer afterwards, so you also\n  detect over-writing.\n- `jsonp_strtod` takes a `strbuffer_t` that must be built with the owning library's\n  `strbuffer_init` + `strbuffer_append_bytes`, and closed with the same library.\n  Compare the return value and `*out` via `to_bits()`.\n\nWrite these tests, covering CONFIGS.md rows 23-35 and ERRORS.md rows 235-243:\n\n1. `dtoa_r_jsonp_dtostr_path` — the exact call `jsonp_dtostr` makes:\n   `dtoa_r(value, 0, 0, &decpt, &sign, &rve, buf, 25)`. Run it over: 0.0, -0.0, 1.0,\n   -1.0, 0.5, 1e-323 (subnormal), f64::MIN_POSITIVE, f64::MAX, f64::MIN, 1e16, 1e17,\n   1e-4, 1e-5, 123456789012345678.0, and 20000 randomized doubles from a seeded `Rng`\n   (use both `rng.finite_f64()` for full-range bit patterns and `rng.tame_f64()`).\n   (CONFIGS 23)\n2. `dtoa_r_all_modes_and_ndigits` — `mode` 0..=9 crossed with `ndigits` in\n   {-5, -1, 0, 1, 2, 5, 15, 17, 30}, over ~400 randomized doubles (seeded) plus the\n   special values above. Use a large `buf` (e.g. 64 bytes) and also repeat with a\n   deliberately SMALL `blen` to exercise the \"buffer too short\" `NULL` return.\n   (CONFIGS 24; ERRORS 238,241)\n3. `dtoa_r_mode_out_of_range` — `mode` = -1, -100, 10, 11, 1000, i32::MIN, i32::MAX\n   (documented as \"treated as mode 0\"), over a set of values.\n   (CONFIGS 25; ERRORS 240)\n4. `dtoa_r_specials` — NaN (several payloads incl. signalling), +inf, -inf: assert\n   `*decpt == 9999` and identical digit strings/sign in both libs.\n   (CONFIGS 27; ERRORS 239)\n5. `dtoa_r_rve_null_and_heap_alloc` — `rve = NULL`; and `buf = NULL, blen = 0` so the\n   result is heap-allocated: compare the string, then `freedtoa` on the OWNING\n   library. Cover ~200 randomized doubles.\n   (CONFIGS 26,29)\n6. `dtoa_static_result_reuse` — `dtoa(v, mode, ndigits, &decpt, &sign, &rve)` called\n   repeatedly (at least 300 times) without freeing, comparing each result: this\n   exercises the internal static-result reuse and its implicit `freedtoa`.\n   (CONFIGS 28)\n7. `gethex_shapes` — hex-float strings: \"0x1p0\", \"0x1.8p3\", \"0xAp-4\", \"0x0p0\",\n   \"0x1.fffffffffffffp+1023\", \"0x1p-1074\", \"0x1p-1075\", \"0x10000000000000000p0\",\n   \"xyz\" (no digits), \"\" (empty), \"0x\", \"0x.8p0\", \"p0\". Cross with `rounding` 0,1,2,3\n   and `sign` 0,1. NOTE: `gethex` expects `*sp` to point just AFTER the \"0x\" prefix in\n   th