 a\n   deliberately SMALL `blen` to exercise the \"buffer too short\" `NULL` return.\n   (CONFIGS 24; ERRORS 238,241)\n3. `dtoa_r_mode_out_of_range` — `mode` = -1, -100, 10, 11, 1000, i32::MIN, i32::MAX\n   (documented as \"treated as mode 0\"), over a set of values.\n   (CONFIGS 25; ERRORS 240)\n4. `dtoa_r_specials` — NaN (several payloads incl. signalling), +inf, -inf: assert\n   `*decpt == 9999` and identical digit strings/sign in both libs.\n   (CONFIGS 27; ERRORS 239)\n5. `dtoa_r_rve_null_and_heap_alloc` — `rve = NULL`; and `buf = NULL, blen = 0` so the\n   result is heap-allocated: compare the string, then `freedtoa` on the OWNING\n   library. Cover ~200 randomized doubles.\n   (CONFIGS 26,29)\n6. `dtoa_static_result_reuse` — `dtoa(v, mode, ndigits, &decpt, &sign, &rve)` called\n   repeatedly (at least 300 times) without freeing, comparing each result: this\n   exercises the internal static-result reuse and its implicit `freedtoa`.\n   (CONFIGS 28)\n7. `gethex_shapes` — hex-float strings: \"0x1p0\", \"0x1.8p3\", \"0xAp-4\", \"0x0p0\",\n   \"0x1.fffffffffffffp+1023\", \"0x1p-1074\", \"0x1p-1075\", \"0x10000000000000000p0\",\n   \"xyz\" (no digits), \"\" (empty), \"0x\", \"0x.8p0\", \"p0\". Cross with `rounding` 0,1,2,3\n   and `sign` 0,1. NOTE: `gethex` expects `*sp` to point just AFTER the \"0x\" prefix in\n   the C's own use, so test BOTH placements (start of string and after \"0x\") — the\n   only requirement is that BOTH libraries get the identical input.\n   (CONFIGS 30; ERRORS 242)\n8. `strtod__unused_shapes` — \"0\", \"1\", \"-1\", \"1.5\", \"1e10\", \"1E-10\", \"1e999\",\n   \"-1e999\", \"1e-999\", \"0x1p3\", \"  12\", \"+3\", \".5\", \"5.\", \"abc\", \"\", \"1e\", \"1e+\",\n   \"inf\", \"nan\", \"infinity\", 300-digit numbers, and 2000 randomized numeric strings\n   built from a seeded `Rng`. Compare with `se` NULL and non-NULL.\n   (CONFIGS 31; ERRORS 243)\n9. `dtoa_divmax_symbol` — the exported data symbol has the same value in both:\n   `unsafe { d.c.data::<i32>(\"dtoa_divmax\") }`. (CONFIGS 32)\n10. `jsonp_dtostr_precisions` — `precision` 0..=31 crossed with 3000 randomized\n    doubles (seeded) plus the special/boundary values, `size` = 25 (what `dump.c`\n    uses). Compare return value and full buffer. Precisions whose output would exceed\n    25 bytes must return -1 in BOTH. (CONFIGS 33; ERRORS 236)\n11. `jsonp_dtostr_buffer_sizes` — for a fixed set of values, `size` = 0,1,2,...,30.\n    Compare return value and full buffer. (CONFIGS 34; ERRORS 236,237)\n12. `jsonp_strtod_values` — strbuffer contents \"0\", \"-0\", \"1\", \"1.5\", \"1e300\",\n    \"1e308\", \"1e309\", \"1e999\", \"-1e999\", \"1e-999\", \"0.0000000000000000001\",\n    a 400-digit integer, plus 2000 randomized numeric strings. Compare return value\n    and `*out` bit pattern. `1e999` must return -1 in BOTH.\n    (CONFIGS 35; ERRORS 235)\n\nIMPORTANT RULES\n- Never call Rust functions directly; only through `d.rs.<name>` function pointers.\n- Use FIXED seeds so runs are reproducible.\n- Do NOT modify anything under `c_src/`, and do NOT modify `tests/common/mod.rs` or\n  any other existing file. Create ONLY `tests/t04_dtoa.rs`.\n- The C is ALWAYS right. If C and Rust diverge, do NOT change the test to hide it —\n  report the divergence precisely (function, inputs, C value, Rust value).\n- Free every heap result with the OWNING library's `freedtoa`/`jsonp_free`.\n\nVERIFY YOUR WORK before finishing:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust\ncargo build 2>&1 | tail -5\ntimeout 600 cargo test --test t04_dtoa 2>&1 | tail -60\n```\nIterate until it COMPILES and all tests either pass or reveal a genuine C/Rust\ndivergence. Keep total runtime under ~180 seconds (tune iteration counts down if\nneeded, but keep randomized coverage in the thousands for the main paths).\n\nReport: the exact file path created, the number of tests, the pass/fail counts from\nthe final `cargo test` run, and a precise list of any C-vs-Rust divergences found.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-hjHD91-translated-rust/0aaf00f6-473d-4ae1-b7a7-2a8b9811f369/tasks/ae21a7d5dc66fbac2.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
