{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cdf4v7ws56gdv47j5goaib67imcss5vqsq74zn7otsyy2ndnjvjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. All 8 tests pass with zero divergences.\n\n## File created\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/tests/t02_strbuffer.rs` (only file created; nothing else touched)\n\n## Final run\n```\nrunning 8 tests\ntest init_and_close_state ... ok\ntest append_bytes_overflow_rejections ... ok\ntest append_byte_growth_boundary ... ok\ntest value_and_steal_value ... ok\ntest pop_behaviour ... ok\ntest clear_then_reuse ... ok\ntest append_bytes_sizes ... ok\ntest append_bytes_randomized_sequences ... ok\n\ntest result: ok. 8 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; finished in 0.02s\n```\n`cargo build` is clean, no warnings. Total runtime ~0.02 s.\n\n## Tests (8) and coverage\n1. `init_and_close_state` — CONFIGS 6: init return, `length=0`, `size=16`, `value[0]=0`, `strbuffer_value == value`, then close (`value=NULL`, `length=0`, `size=0`) plus an idempotent second close.\n2. `append_byte_growth_boundary` — CONFIGS 7: 40 single-byte appends with a snapshot after every one; 0x00/0x7F/0x80/0xFF placed at indices 14,15,16,30,31,32 so they straddle the growth points. Confirms C growth schedule 16→32 (at `length==15`) →64 (at `length==31`), final `length=40, size=64`.\n3. `append_bytes_sizes` — CONFIGS 8: sizes 0,1,2,15,16,17,31,32,100,1000,10000, two consecutive appends each, seeded payloads with forced embedded NULs every 7th byte plus 0x7F/0x80/0xFF; also asserts C content byte-for-byte against the expected concatenation + NUL.\n4. `append_bytes_randomized_sequences` — CONFIGS 8: 400 seeded sequences × 1..29 appends × 0..200 bytes (one in four chunks all-NUL), snapshot compared after every append (~6000 appends).\n5. `pop_behaviour` — CONFIGS 9 / ERRORS 210: N in 0,1,2,16,17,100, `N+3` pops, comparing both the returned `char` (also against the value predicted from the C source) and the snapshot; covers `length==0 → '\\0'`, then reuses the emptied buffer.\n6. `clear_then_reuse` — CONFIGS 10: 0/1/100/10000 initial bytes, clear (asserts single NUL byte, `size` retained), re-append, clear again, two more appends.\n7. `value_and_steal_value` — CONFIGS 11 / ERRORS 211: `strbuffer_value` contents, steal (bytes of the stolen block, `value==NULL`, `length`/`size` **unchanged** — matching the C, which only nulls `value`), `strbuffer_value` returns NULL afterwards, second steal returns NULL in both, stolen pointers freed with the owning library's `jsonp_free`, then `strbuffer_close`.\n8. `append_bytes_overflow_rejections` — ERRORS 207/208/209: fresh-buffer `usize::MAX` and `usize::MAX-1`, plus five hand-built `strbuffer_t`s (return value + \"struct and 64-byte block untouched\" only).\n\n## Notable C-semantics findings (asserted, not worked around)\n- `strbuffer_steal_value` leaves `length` and `size` **unchanged** (only `value` is nulled), despite the header comment \"Steal the value and close the strbuffer\". Both libs agree; the test asserts the actual C behaviour.\n- The suggested hand-built case `length=SIZE_MAX-8, size=SIZE_MAX-4` does **not** reach the `length > SIZE_MAX-1-size` guard — `strbuff->size > SIZE_MAX/2` fires first. I kept it (labelled as guard 209) and added two cases that genuinely hit guard 208: `(length=SIZE_MAX-100, size=16, append=200)` and `(length=2^62, size=SIZE_MAX/2, append=SIZE_MAX-2^62)`. Guard triggering was verified independently by re-deriving the branch conditions; all three guards are exercised.\n- `strbuffer_append_bytes(fresh, p, usize::MAX-1)` passes **all three** guards (`length(0) > SIZE_MAX-1-size` is `0 > 0`, false) and is rejected only by the failing `jsonp_realloc(value, 16, SIZE_MAX)`. Both libraries return -1 and leave state untouched; documented in a comment in the test.\n\n## Divergences\nNone. C and Rust agreed on every return value and every `(length, size, bytes)` snapshot across all ~19k compared operations."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":80715,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":393,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WcvaMYNMfrR18TTx6dMBBY","session_id":"0aaf00f6-473d-4ae1-b7a7-2a8b9811f369","uuid":"a000eb5c-ed58-45b2-8b3a-e160ccaba35b","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:35:56.282Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write strbuffer differential tests"}
