{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pkeztdahf4bgitrrm67w5xbrffphjceoirblnycgzdvhgvkgek4q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## File created\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/tests/t01_utf.rs` (only file created; nothing else modified)\n\n## Result\n\n```\nrunning 7 tests\ntest result: ok. 7 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 1.02s\n```\n\n`cargo build` is clean (no warnings, no errors). Total runtime ~1.0 s.\n\n## The 7 tests\n\n| test | coverage |\n|---|---|\n| `utf8_check_first_all_256_bytes` | all 256 byte values (CONFIGS 1; ERRORS 214/215/216) + a guard that the C and Rust symbols resolve to distinct addresses (no interposition) |\n| `utf8_encode_boundaries` | the 20 specified codepoints; compares return, whole 8-byte `0xAA`-sentinel buffer, and `*size` (sentinel `usize::MAX`) (CONFIGS 3; ERRORS 212/213) |\n| `utf8_encode_randomized` | 20000 random `i32` (seed `0xA1`) **plus an exhaustive sweep of every codepoint `0..=0x1100FF`** plus 20000 random above-range values (seed `0xA2`) |\n| `utf8_check_full_sizes_and_randomized` | `size` 0..=6 × 2000 random 8-byte buffers per size (seed `0xB1`, half biased toward real lead/continuation bytes), `*codepoint` sentinel `-12345`, plus the `codepoint == NULL` branch; **plus all 65536 two-byte sequences at `size == 2`** (CONFIGS 2; ERRORS 217-221) |\n| `utf8_check_full_handcrafted` | 29 explicit sequences (valid 2/3/4-byte, overlong `C0 80`/`E0 80 80`/`F0 80 80 80`, surrogates `ED A0 80`/`ED BF BF`, above-range `F4 90 80 80`/`F7 BF BF BF`, bad continuation `C2 41`/`E2 82 41`, …) × 2 padding bytes × `size` 0..=6 |\n| `utf8_iterate_all_shapes` | 30 shapes (valid 1/2/3/4-byte, invalid leads, truncated, check_full failures, multi-char buffers) × 2 pads × `bufsize` {0,1,2,3,4,len,8}; 3000 random buffers (seed `0xC1`) × `bufsize` {0,1,2,3,4,8}; **plus all 65536 two-byte buffers at `bufsize` 1 and 2**. Compares NULL-ness first, then the returned pointer as an offset from the shared buffer, then `*codepoint`, and repeats every case with `codepoint = NULL` (CONFIGS 4; ERRORS 222-225) |\n| `utf8_check_string_shapes` | len 0 / len 1; every single byte value; all prefixes of `\"hello world\"` and of `\"ab<euro>cd\"` (len shorter than the real buffer, len 0 with non-empty buffer); 2000 random ASCII len 1..64 (seed `0xD1`); 5000 random byte buffers len 1..64 (seed `0xD2`) each also at a shorter len; 2000 valid `Rng::utf8_string` values truncated by 1/2/3 bytes and with an embedded NUL spliced in (seed `0xD3`); 7 explicit embedded-NUL shapes at every len plus the `cbuf`-terminated form; **plus all 65536 two-byte strings at len 1 and 2** (CONFIGS 5; ERRORS 226-228) |\n\nAll `Rng` instances use fixed hex seeds. All buffers are 8-byte padded (`padded8`) so every `bufsize`/`size` passed to the C is in bounds; helper asserts enforce that (`utf8_check_full` dereferences `buffer[0]` unconditionally, so buffers are never empty).\n\nEach test also contains **absolute ground-truth assertions against the C only** (derived from `c_src/src/utf.c`), e.g. `utf8_encode(0x10348) -> F0 90 8D 88` with the remaining sentinel bytes untouched, `*size` untouched on the two `-1` paths, `utf8_check_full` not writing `*codepoint` on failure, and `utf8_iterate(buf, 0, cp)` returning `buf` unchanged without touching `*codepoint`. These prevent the pair from \"agreeing on garbage\" and confirm the loops actually execute. All of them hold for the C.\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**None.** C and Rust agree on every input exercised, including the exhaustive codepoint sweep for `utf8_encode` and the exhaustive 2-byte matrices for `utf8_check_full`, `utf8_iterate` and `utf8_check_string`. `src/utf.rs` is a faithful transliteration; the only cosmetic difference (`value` is `0`-initialised in Rust vs uninitialised in C in `utf8_iterate`) is unobservable because every path that reaches `*