{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_36qpd55k5j2xzxmmfnayz24qohb5667stjcl7y6d73zrczkmb4zq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## File created\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/tests/t04_dtoa.rs` (1082 lines, the only file created or modified)\n\n## Tests: 12\n`dtoa_r_jsonp_dtostr_path`, `dtoa_r_all_modes_and_ndigits`, `dtoa_r_mode_out_of_range`, `dtoa_r_specials`, `dtoa_r_rve_null_and_heap_alloc`, `dtoa_static_result_reuse`, `gethex_shapes`, `strtod__unused_shapes`, `dtoa_divmax_symbol`, `jsonp_dtostr_precisions`, `jsonp_dtostr_buffer_sizes`, `jsonp_strtod_values` — mapping 1:1 onto CONFIGS.md rows 23-35 and ERRORS.md rows 235-243.\n\n## Final result\n```\ncargo build   -> Finished (clean, no warnings from the new file)\ncargo test --test t04_dtoa\n  test result: ok. 12 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; finished in 1.43s   (wall 1.86s)\n```\n\n## C-vs-Rust divergences found\n**None.** Every compared observable was byte-identical: return NULL-ness, the NUL-terminated digit string, `*decpt`, `*sign`, `*rve` as an offset from the returned pointer, the entire 0xAA-prefilled caller buffer *plus a 16-byte guard region past `blen`/`size`*, `gethex`'s `*sp` offset and `*rvp` raw bit pattern, `strtod__unused`'s result bits and `*se` offset, `jsonp_dtostr`'s return value + whole buffer, and `jsonp_strtod`'s return value + `*out` bits.\n\nCoverage actually driven (both `.so`s, fixed seeds): ~40 000 values on the `jsonp_dtostr` `dtoa_r` path; 2 414 values × mode 0..9 × ndigits {-5,-1,0,1,2,5,15,17,30} × 3 `blen` regimes (~1.3 M `dtoa_r` calls); 268 values × 7 out-of-range modes; 4 025 `gethex` inputs × rounding 0..3 × sign 0/1 × 2 pointer placements; ~2 050 `strtod__unused` strings × `se` NULL/non-NULL; 6 014 values × precision 0..31 for `jsonp_dtostr`; 33 values × size 0..30 × 8 precisions; ~2 028 `jsonp_strtod` buffers; 523 `dtoa` calls exercising static-result reuse.\n\n## Notable findings / decisions\n- **Divergence detection was verified by mutation**: I temporarily perturbed one argument in each comparison helper (`dr_buf`, `dr_heap`, `dtoa_call`, `dtostr`, `gethex_one`, `strtod_one`, `strtod_sb`) and confirmed every one produced a loud `C vs RUST divergence` failure, then reverted. So the passes are real, not vacuous.\n- **`dtoa.c` is not thread-safe** (compiled without `MULTIPLE_THREADS`: `dtoa_result`, the `Balloc`/`Bfree` free list and `p5s` are plain mutable statics). Cargo's parallel test threads would race on them, so every test in the file takes one process-wide `Mutex`.\n- **`gethex` unconditionally reads `*sp + 2`** (it assumes it is being handed a pointer at a `0x` prefix). Short inputs like `\"\"`, `\"0x\"`, `\"p0\"` therefore read past the terminator, so all `gethex` inputs are padded with 16 trailing NULs — identical memory for both libraries, no out-of-bounds read.\n- **`jsonp_dtostr(precision >= 25)` returns -1 only for finite non-zero values.** `±0.0`, NaN and `±Inf` leave `dtoa_r` through `nrv_alloc` *before* the `blen <= i` check, so they still succeed with `size = 25` (e.g. `0.0` returns 3). Both libraries agree; my first draft asserted -1 unconditionally and the C correctly refuted it.\n- **Translation difference worth flagging (not exercised, deliberately):** C's `jsonp_strtod` contains `assert(end == strbuffer->value + strbuffer->length)` and the CMake build defines no `NDEBUG`, so the assert is live; the Rust `src/strconv.rs::jsonp_strtod` **omits it**. For a strbuffer that `strtod` does not fully consume (e.g. `\"1e\"`), C would `abort()` while Rust returns 0. I kept every `jsonp_strtod` input fully consumable so the C process cannot abort — testing that case would kill the test binary rather than report a comparison.\n- Unrelated pre-existing failure: `cargo test` (whole suite) aborts in `tests/t06_load.rs::loaders_with_null_error_struct` with a thread stack overflow. That file is untouched by me and is a separate test binary; `--test t04_dtoa` is unaffected."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_read_input_tokens":125671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1652,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012kCimBgXy76kS5iXvx3Bku","session_id":"0aaf00f6-473d-4ae1-b7a7-2a8b9811f369","uuid":"7cc05fd1-97ed-4060-9483-a00274b3adfe","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:41:58.992Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write dtoa/strconv differential tests"}
