/common/mod.rs        (the harness — read it fully)\n- .../translated_rust/tests/t00_smoke.rs         (see `valist_construction_works`)\n- .../translated_rust/tests/t05_value.rs         (see the `V` enum / `build2` / `same` pattern)\n- .../translated_rust/c_src/src/pack_unpack.c    (the C ground truth — read it fully)\n- .../translated_rust/CONFIGS.md rows 112-128 and ERRORS.md rows 157-199\n\nYOUR TASK: create exactly one new file\n  /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/tests/t08_pack.rs\n\nStart with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\n```\n\n## Harness facts you need\n\n`duo()` -> `&'static Duo` with `.c` / `.rs` (`Lib`). Relevant declarations:\n```rust\njson_pack:       unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, ...) -> *mut json_t,\njson_pack_ex:    unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut json_error_t, usize, *const c_char, ...) -> *mut json_t,\njson_vpack_ex:   unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut json_error_t, usize, *const c_char, *mut VaListTag) -> *mut json_t,\njson_unpack:     unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut json_t, *const c_char, ...) -> c_int,\njson_unpack_ex:  unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut json_t, *mut json_error_t, usize, *const c_char, ...) -> c_int,\njson_vunpack_ex: unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut json_t, *mut json_error_t, usize, *const c_char, *mut VaListTag) -> c_int,\n```\nplus every `json_*` value function, `json_dumps`, `jsonp_free`, and the helpers\n`json_error_t::new()/snapshot()/raw()/code()`, `eq`, `eq_bytes`, `eq_err`,\n`describe(&Lib, *const json_t)`, `decref(&Lib, *mut json_t)`, `incref`, `cs`,\n`cbuf`, `cstr_bytes`, `Rng`, `dumps_both`.\n\n### Building `va_list` arguments — this is the key mechanism\n`VaArgs` builds a REAL x86-64 SysV `va_list` whose arguments all come from the\noverflow area, i.e. a flat array of 8-byte slots consumed in order:\n```rust\nlet mut va = VaArgs::new()\n    .ptr(key_cstring.as_ptr())   // const char*\n    .int(42)                     // C `int`\n    .i64(1234567890123i64)       // json_int_t\n    .usize(7)                    // size_t\n    .f64(1.5)                    // double\n    .ptr_mut(&mut out as *mut _); // any out-pointer\nlet ap = va.build();             // *mut VaListTag, valid while `va` lives\nlet j = (l.json_vpack_ex)(std::ptr::null_mut(), 0, fmt.as_ptr(), ap);\n```\nIMPORTANT: `va.build()` must be called once, after all args are pushed, and\n`va` must stay alive for the whole call. Build a SEPARATE `VaArgs` for the C\ncall and for the Rust call (the callee advances the list).\n`t00_smoke.rs::valist_construction_works` is a working example — copy its shape.\n\nPrefer `json_vpack_ex` / `json_vunpack_ex` (the low-level entry points) for the\nbulk of the coverage, and ALSO exercise the variadic wrappers `json_pack`,\n`json_pack_ex`, `json_unpack`, `json_unpack_ex` directly with real Rust\nvariadic calls (e.g. `(l.json_pack)(fmt.as_ptr(), 1i32, s.as_ptr())`) — those\nwrappers are implemented in the Rust with hand-written naked assembly\n(`src/va.rs`), so they MUST be tested through the `.so`.\n\n### Comparison rules\n- Pack: compare NULL-ness of the result, then `describe(&d.c, cj)` vs\n  `describe(&d.rs, rj)`, then `dumps_both(d, cj, rj, JSON_ENCODE_ANY|JSON_SORT_KEYS)`\n  byte-for-byte, then `eq_err(...)` on the two `json_error_t`s.\n- Unpack: compare the `c_int` return, `eq_err(...)`, AND every out-parameter you\n  passed (int / json_int_t / double bits / `const char*` contents / `size_t`\n  length / `json_t*` — for `json_t*` out-params compare `describe(...)` of the\n  pointed-to value, never the raw pointer). Also compare the ROOT afterwards\n  (`describe`) since `O` increments its refcount.\n- Values that must exist in both libraries have to be built with the OWNING\n  library's constructors (see `t05_value.rs::build2`).\n\n## Coverage required\n\nCONFIGS.md rows 112-128:\n112 every single pack format char: `{}`, `[]`, `s`, `n`, `b`, `i`, `I`, `f`, `o`, `O`\n113 `json_pack_ex`/`json_vpack_ex` with `error` NULL and non-NULL, flags 0\n114 `s#` (int length), `s%` (size_t length), `s+`, `s+#`, `s+%` concatenation —\n    include lengths shorter than strlen, 0, and multi-part concatenations\n115 optional `s?`, `s*`, `o?`, `o*`, `O?`, `O*` with NULL and non-NULL args\n116 nested `{s:{s:[i,i,i]}}` 3 levels; 0 / 1 / many members\n117 whitespace and `,` / `:` separators sprinkled through the format string\n118 `b` with 0 and non-zero; `i` with `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`/0; `I` with `INT64_MIN`/`INT64_MAX`\n119 `f` with randomized finite doubles (seeded `Rng`), plus 0.0/-0.0\n120 every unpack format char against a matching root: `{}`,`[]`,`s`,`i`,`I`,`b`,`f`,`F`,`o`,`O`,`n`\n121 `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` (no varargs consumed at all)\n122 `JSON_STRICT` with exact / extra object keys and array elements\n123 `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY | JSON_STRICT`\n124 in-format `!` and `*` strictness markers in objects and arrays\n125 optional `s?` object keys, present and absent\n126 `s%` string + length; `o` / `O` and their refcount effect (compare the root's\n    refcount after the call — `describe` already prints refcounts)\n127 nested `{s:[i,i]}` 3 levels; the \"skipping\" path where `root == NULL`\n    internally (reached via an absent optional key `s?` whose sub-format is a\n    container, e.g. `{s?:[i,i]}` against an object lacking that key)\n128 pack -> unpack round trip over randomized format strings (seeded)\n\nERRORS.md rows 157-199 — EVERY row needs a test that constructs exactly that\ncondition and asserts C and Rust return the SAME code/sentinel. Read the table\nin ERRORS.md; it lists the function, trigger and expected result for each. They\ncover: NULL string args, invalid UTF-8 args, `s?`/`s*` combined with `#`/`%`/`+`,\n`pack_object`/`pack_array` unexpected end of format, non-`s` key spec, NULL\nobject value with/without `*`, NULL `o`/`O` arg without `?`/`*`, NaN/Inf for `f`,\nunknown format chars, NULL/empty `fmt`, garbage after format, and for unpack:\nwrong root type for every specifier, `!`/`*` misplacement, NULL key, missing\nobject item, strict leftovers (object and array), array index out of range,\nNULL `const char**` / `size_t*` targets, NULL root, and garbage after format.\n\nAlso cover generically (even though not in the table):\n- flags with unknown/reserved bits set (`1<<20`, `1<<40`, `usize::MAX`) — must be\n  ignored identically;\n- format strings that are pure whitespace, only separators (`\" , : \"`), extremely\n  long, and containing every byte 0x01..0x7F as the single format char;\n- randomized garbage format strings (a few thousand, seeded) driven through\n  `json_vpack_ex` and `json_vunpack_ex` with a generous `VaArgs` full of harmless\n  values (valid pointers to short C strings, zeros, and a real `json_t*`), so the\n  C never dereferences anything invalid but every parse path is hit.\n\n## IMPORTANT RULES\n- Never call Rust functions directly; only through `d.rs.<name>` pointers.\n- Use FIXED seeds.\n- Do NOT modify anything under `c_src/`, and do NOT modify `tests/common/mod.rs`\n  or any other existing file. Create ONLY `tests/t08_pack.rs`.\n- The C is ALWAYS right. If C and Rust diverge, do NOT change the test to hide\n  it — report the divergence precisely (function, format string, args, C result,\n  Rust result).\n- Avoid leaking; `decref` every value you create. For `pack` failures the C may\n  or may not have consumed a reference — follow the C source.\n- Some tests may need a bigger thread stack for deeply nested formats; if so,\n  wrap the test body like `tests/t06_load.rs` does with its `big_stack` helper\n  (define your own local copy; do not touch t06).\n\n## VERIFY before finishing\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust\ncargo build 2>&1 | tail -5\ntimeout 600 cargo test --test t08_pack 2>&1 | tail -60\n```\nIterate until it COMPILES and all tests either pass or reveal a genuine\ndivergence. Keep runtime under ~180 seconds.\n\nReport: the file path, the number of tests, the final pass/fail counts, a mapping\nof which CONFIGS/ERRORS rows each test covers, and a precise list of any\nC-vs-Rust divergences found.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-hjHD91-translated-rust/0aaf00f6-473d-4ae1-b7a7-2a8b9811f369/tasks/af0e653889ebbc7ee.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
