{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mat5hziz6fm4hkgsgc5633ik6mj74xlva3aro52izkyy4iiipdua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Final state verified.\n\n## File created\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjHD91/translated_rust/tests/t03_hashtable.rs` (the only file I created or modified)\n\n## Results\n\n**12 tests, 12 passed, 0 failed**, in 0.91 s (whole workspace suite: 83 tests, all pass, 4.8 s).\n\n```\nrunning 12 tests\ntest init_state ... ok                        test del_positions ... ok\ntest set_counts_and_rehash ... ok             test clear_and_reuse ... ok\ntest set_overwrite_existing ... ok            test iteration_full_traversal ... ok\ntest key_shapes ... ok                        test iter_at_resume ... ok\ntest get_present_and_absent ... ok            test iter_set_replaces_value ... ok\ntest randomized_operation_sequences ... ok    test long_key_rejection ... ok\ntest result: ok. 12 passed; 0 failed; ... finished in 0.91s\n```\n\n## C-vs-Rust divergences found\n\n**None.** Every return value, `size`, `order`, key/key_len/value and full iteration order matched exactly across all tests.\n\n## Key findings\n\n**1. ERRORS 231 (`init_pair` overflow guard) is unreachable in both implementations.** `hashtable_set` does `hash = hash_str(key, key_len)` *before* calling `init_pair`, and `hashlittle()` reads `key_len` bytes. So any `key_len` near `SIZE_MAX - offsetof(pair_t,key)` walks off the buffer and kills the process before the guard can return `-1`. I probed this in forked children; for `key_len` ∈ {`SIZE_MAX`, `SIZE_MAX-8`, `SIZE_MAX-56`, `SIZE_MAX-57`} **both** libraries die with SIGSEGV (signal 11) — identical, so no divergence, but the documented `-1` is not observable. To actually cover `hashtable_set`'s `if (!pair) return -1;` I added a forked probe that installs an always-failing `jsonp_malloc` via `json_set_alloc_funcs`; both libraries return `-1` there.\n\n**2. Iteration order is *insertion* order, not hash order.** `hashtable_iter*` walks `ordered_list`, so comparing iteration order pins down the `ordered_list` splicing but is **blind to the bucket chain** (`hashtable->list`, `bucket->first/last`) — a corrupted chain would iterate perfectly. I closed that gap by pairing every snapshot with `hashtable_get` sweeps over all keys that must be present plus all keys that must be gone (in `del_positions` and in every step of the randomized test).\n\n**3. `lookup3.h`'s `hashlittle()` cannot be validated through this API.** `hashtable_find_pair` compares the *stored* `pair->hash` with a freshly computed one, so a self-consistent but different hash behaves identically. Note the Rust uses the byte-at-a-time path unconditionally while the C uses 32/16-bit aligned reads with the masking trick — the tests hand the *identical* key pointer to both libraries so the alignment-dependent paths are exercised in parallel, but the result is structurally unobservable. `hashlittle` is `static` in the C, so it isn't dlsym-able either; only `hashtable_seed` parity is checkable (already done in `t00_smoke.rs`).\n\n**4. Rehash timing corrected.** The first rehash happens on the **9th** insert, not the 8th (the load check uses the pre-insert `size`). Verified against the C: `order == 3` for n ≤ 8, else the smallest k with n ≤ 2^k. `hashtable_clear` and deletion never shrink `order`.\n\n**5. CONFIGS 22 (several distinct seeds) is not exercisable in-process** — `json_object_seed` is a one-shot no-op once the seed is non-zero, and per the harness both libraries are fixed at `TEST_SEED`. Given finding 3, varying the seed would add no discriminating power anyway.\n\n## Test-effectiveness check (mutation testing)\n\nTo confirm the assertions really bite, I temporarily perturbed the harness and reverted: dropping the first entry from the Rust snapshot failed **11 of 12** tests (only `init_state`, whose tables are empty, was unaffected); forcing the Rust `hashtable_get` to always miss failed **8 of 12**. The file is back to its passing state."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":756,"cache_read_input_tokens":147479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":756,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TfJ2ptRDhUxQLatYnis5yh","session_id":"0aaf00f6-473d-4ae1-b7a7-2a8b9811f369","uuid":"17dc0d37-059a-45f6-bfdc-e33f4b03dd60","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:44:56.172Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write hashtable differential tests"}
