a `catch_unwind`, then re-verified with `json_get_alloc_funcs2` before the panic is re-raised.\n- Every custom hook delegates to libc `malloc`/`realloc`/`free`, and each library's blocks are only ever freed through that same library.\n- `json_object_seed` is tested **only** as a no-op (values 12345, 1, 0xFFFFFFFF, TEST_SEED, usize::MAX, 0x1_0000_0000), asserting `hashtable_seed` is unchanged, equal across libraries, and equal to `TEST_SEED`. The auto-seed path is not touched.\n\n## Notable verified facts (all C == Rust)\n- Default hooks on **both** `.so`s are the *same* addresses as the test executable's libc `malloc`/`realloc`/`free` (the canonical-PLT definition, so `extern \"C\"` address-taking is directly comparable).\n- `json_set_alloc_funcs` leaves `do_realloc == NULL` on both; the emulation call sequence is byte-exactly `malloc(16) malloc(48) free malloc(8) free free malloc(64) free` on both, matching `memory.c` line-for-line, with `min(old,new)` copy contents verified.\n- **Allocation call sequences match element-for-element** on all six workloads: emulation 100-key object **1050** events, emulation load/dump/deep_copy **424**, counting load/dump/deep_copy **409**, counting 100-key object **1042**, counting 1000-element array **2027**, counting `JSON_SORT_KEYS` dumps **359**. (Verified non-vacuous by temporary instrumentation, since removed.)\n- `error.c` truncation: all 252 bytes compared with `eq_err` after every call, on 0x00/0xAA/0xFF-prefilled structs, so *untouched* bytes are also checked. `source` truncation validated against an independently computed `expect_source()` ground truth (`\"...\"` + 76-byte tail + NUL) for lengths 0,1,2,40,78,79,80,81,82,83,100,159,200,500.\n- `jsonp_error_vset`: 8 message lengths × 30 codes (0..=17 plus 18, 99, 127, 128, 200, 255, 256, 257, −1, −128, −129, `i32::MIN`, `i32::MAX`) = 240 cases; `text[158] == 0`, `text[159] == code as u8`, truncation at 158 chars, `position` truncated to `int` (incl. `usize::MAX`, `0x1_2345_6789`) — all identical.\n- `jsonp_error_set` (naked-asm variadic): `%s %d %% %c %x %X %#x %u %ld %f %g %e`, 6-arg mixed, 8-pointer overflow-area, float args (`al != 0` / xmm save area), 158-char truncation, out-of-range codes, already-set no-overwrite, `error == NULL` — all identical.\n- `jansson_version_cmp`: 48 fixed triples + 4000 seeded random triples (seed `0x0913_4C4D_5001_2345`, incl. `i32::MIN`/`i32::MAX` so the raw wrapping difference is compared) — exact `int` match everywhere.\n- `jsonp_strndup(str, SIZE_MAX)` returns NULL in both (confirmed against `memory.c`: `jsonp_malloc(len + 1)` sees size 0, returns NULL, short-circuiting before the `memcpy`).\n\n## Divergences found\n**None.** No C-vs-Rust difference was observed in `memory.c`, `version.c`, `hashtable_seed.c` or `error.c`, including the allocation-sequence equivalence checks."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1006,"cache_read_input_tokens":143932,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1006,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EKktdTFVDzSmnHvauf8Hi4","session_id":"0aaf00f6-473d-4ae1-b7a7-2a8b9811f369","uuid":"5478bef4-474e-4d0e-99cc-b085632899c4","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:58:49.065Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write memory/error/version tests"}
